Do not flip when no new buffer has been swapped

With the refresh lock (WESTEROS_GL_USE_REFRESH_LOCK) a swap waits for the
refresh thread and marks its window dirty only when it is let go. A swap that
comes in before the flip of the previous one is shown by that flip already
(the front buffer is the newest one), and the window is then marked dirty
once more with nothing new behind it. The next flip got no buffer from
gbm_surface_lock_front_buffer and took the handle of none: the process ended
on signal 11 in the refresh thread (wstVRefresh). This happens as soon as the
compositor draws faster than the refresh thread comes round, which RDK's
window manager does at a pace above 60. The atomic path has the check; this
adds it to the other one, which a device without atomic mode setting for
its plane uses.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/westeros-gl/westeros-gl.c b/westeros-gl/westeros-gl.c
index 90082f2..c64cf9d 100644
--- a/westeros-gl/westeros-gl.c
+++ b/westeros-gl/westeros-gl.c
@@ -7045,12 +7045,26 @@ static void wstSwapDRMBuffers( WstGLCtx *ctx )
          if ( nw->dirty )
          {
             TRACE3("nw %p dirty", nw);
-            nw->prevBo= nw->bo;
-            nw->prevFbId= nw->fbId;
             gs= (struct gbm_surface*)nw->nativeWindow;
             if ( gs )
             {
                bo= gbm_surface_lock_front_buffer(gs);
+               if ( !bo )
+               {
+                  /* Nothing has been swapped since the last flip: with the
+                     refresh lock a window is marked dirty when its swap is
+                     let go, which is after the flip that showed it if the
+                     swap came in before that flip. There is nothing new to
+                     show, and no buffer to take a handle of. */
+                  nw->dirty= false;
+                  nw= nw->next;
+                  continue;
+               }
+            }
+            nw->prevBo= nw->bo;
+            nw->prevFbId= nw->fbId;
+            if ( gs )
+            {
                wstUpdateResources( WSTRES_BO_GRAPHICS, true, (long long)bo, __LINE__);
 
                handle= gbm_bo_get_handle(bo).u32;
